# alias: DOPIROPI
# button-text: DOPI-ROPI
# gib-works: false
# bba-works: true
# auction-filter: 4N =.= +[X5]
# vulnerable: NS
# convention-card-ns: 21GF-DEFAULT
# convention-card-ew: 21GF-DEFAULT

/*@chat
--- DOPI-ROPI: Responding to Blackwood after Interference, stick with your response structure 
and just replace the first 2 steps with X/XX and Pass.
https://www.acblunit390.org/Simon/dopi-ropi.htm
@chat*/

# Note: BBA does not implement lead-directing (Lightner) doubles. An
# earlier version used 7-card AKQJ holdings hoping BBA would X 4NT
# for the lead — it never did. This deck instead targets the DOPI
# trigger: opponents bidding 5-level over our 4NT.
#
# BBA's opponents save over 4NT mostly when they are not vulnerable
# against vulnerable: with rotating vulnerability the trigger fired on
# ~1% of deals, at NS-only ~5%, and ~9% once the overcall path below
# was dropped. Hence `# vulnerable: NS` in the header.

# DOPI-ROPI: Interference over Blackwood
dealer north

##### Imported Script -- GIB 1 Notrump #####

ntP = hcp(north) + shape(north,5xxx+x5xx)
nt1 = shape(north, any 5332+any 4432+any 4333) and hcp(north)>14 and ntP<18
nt2 = shape(north, any 5422-5xxx-x5xx-4xxx) and hcp(north)>14 and hcp(north)<17
gibNT = nt1 or nt2

### End of GIB 1 Notrump ###

# N/S slam zone
slamZone = hcp(south)>=12 and (hcp(north)+hcp(south))>=28

# === 3-level minor preempt by West, East supports ===
# N opens 1M, S has 4+ support → Jacoby 2NT GF, gives N/S a clean
# path to Blackwood. W preempts a 7+ minor (3 of AKQJ); E has 4+
# support so W has confidence to compete over 4NT.
# Tried mirror (E-preempter, W-supporter): 0 matches — BBA can't
# navigate from a 2nd-seat 3-level overcall to 4NT.
# Tried requiring partner to lack a 4-card major: hurt match rate.
heartOpen = hearts(north)>4 and hearts(south)>3
spadeOpen = spades(north)>4 and spades(south)>3
majorFit = (heartOpen or spadeOpen) and not gibNT

wClubsLong    = clubs(west)>=7    and top4(west,clubs)>=3
wDiamondsLong = diamonds(west)>=7 and top4(west,diamonds)>=3
wMinor   = wClubsLong or wDiamondsLong
wRange   = hcp(west)>=6 and hcp(west)<=11
wShort   = (spadeOpen and spades(west)<=1) or (heartOpen and hearts(west)<=1)
eFit     = (wClubsLong and clubs(east)>=4) or (wDiamondsLong and diamonds(east)>=4)
eMin     = hcp(east)<10
preemptPath = majorFit and wMinor and wRange and wShort and eFit and eMin

# A second path — E/W with an 11+ major fit overcalling at the 1-level or
# with Unusual NT — was tried and dropped: BBA passed 4NT on ~98% of those
# deals, and they crowded out the preempts.

slamZone and preemptPath

action
average "hcp north       " hcp(north),
average "hcp south       " hcp(south),
average "hcp e+w         " (hcp(east)+hcp(west)),
average "west clubs      " 100 * wClubsLong,
average "west diamonds   " 100 * wDiamondsLong,
